the batman is finally here and based on  fan reaction and critical consensus it  will certainly stand the test of time as  one of the all-time great dark knight  stories but some fans aren't amused by  one major cameo spoilers ahead now that  the batman is out and people have had  time to marinate on it for a little  while it's not above criticism no movie  is perfect and superhero fans have never  had any problem letting their feelings  be known when they believe a work of art  can do better and plenty of people have  already taken to reddit to talk about  that big cameo toward the end of the  film after riddler is locked up in  arkham he speaks to his next-door  cellmate this individual never reveals a  name and in the credits they're listed  as unseen arkham prisoner but it's  pretty obvious who it's meant to be  you can call me  joker  the unseen arkham prisoner played by  barry keoghan references clowns and  laughs maniacally at the end of his  speech in any other superhero movie this  would be a tease that the joker will be  the villain in the next sequel but there  are plenty of fans who believe the  sequel would be better suited with a  different antagonist one redditor  kickstarted a thread talking about how  there have been too many jokers as of  late saying batman has the most distinct  and varied gallery of villains and yet  we are doing the joker again barry  kyogen who is great at anything is the  third live action joker in six years i  wish we could get villains that weren't  properly explored in movies yet the  jokers he's referring to are jared leto  in suicide squad and zack snyder's  justice league plus joaquin phoenix and  joker it's a lot of the same so to avoid  people burning out on joker's  shenanigans some people believe the  batman 2 would be better off exploring  new characters still there are those who  thought kyogen could have been someone  else entirely with one fellow redditer  writing according to the teaser website  from the post credits scene it seems  that barry kyogen might actually be hush  hush is an oft-ignored batman rogue  who's actually thomas elliott and he was  hinted at in the film itself when bruce  wayne learns what his father did to a  reporter we discovered the reporter's  last name was elliot now we know barry  keoghan won't be hush director matt  reeves has already shot that idea down  reeves revealed that the unseen arkham  prisoner is in fact the joker albeit a  prototype version who may not  necessarily be fully formed at this  point it's possible reeves just wanted  audiences to know that the joker is in  this universe but he may not inherently  be the big bad of the sequel in the  follow-up perhaps we'll get a version of  a deleted scene which reeves describes  like this it's a scene where batman is  so unnerved because the riddler is  writing to him and he's like well why is  this guy writing to me and he figures  he's got to profile this killer he goes  to see another killer that he's clearly  had an experience with in these first  two years the killer in question is the  joker in a scene that reeves compares to  silence of the lambs could we see a  scene like it play out in the batman 2  where bruce wayne is at the end of his  rope with hush so he turns to another  madman to stop him batman has an  expansive rogues gallery and fans have  speculated a future villain could be  anyone from mr freeze to the court of  owls it's a big universe out there and  it's clear the newest version of the  caped crusader is just getting started  there are many directions a sequel could  go in and for a subset of fans they'd  love to see the road less traveled check  out one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about the  batman are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

